    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 3269 'Hot Springs Haven' (title), 204 (card), objective 76355; icon 316."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "data/content/dungeons/hot_springs_haven.json: difficulty 1, zone 'Snowhill', enemies ['Umari', 'Champion Pengubowler', 'Yeti Bouncer', 'Yeti Jam Boxes', 'Umari', 'Champion Pengubowler']."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Door at [263.66, 51.69, 164.31]: BJX fork Battles.lua:6 (Npcs.json Id 46185, cave_entrance_facade_01_ice.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region Snowhill, place Snowhill."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 7 ('Hot Springs Haven (the live dungeon: yetis lounging through the resort, Umari in the far lounge)'): scene sh_yeti_cave, entry, exit, 8 waves, 24 spawns ({'Yeti': 7, 'Cave Yeti': 8, 'Yeti Bouncer': 8, 'Umari': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1206 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sh_yeti_cave has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 15 coins / 100 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier. Door actor 100000046185: reference Npcs.json Id 46185, model 10907, name 3269, at [263.66, 51.69, 164.31]."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) The guide's main goal is the one goal shown from the start and is done with the fork's last goal; the steps before it stay, as the triggers of its waves and boss."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Guide overlay by scripts/dungeon_fights.py from data/content/dungeons/hot_springs_haven.json."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): the Yetis that fight wear model 51 sasquatch_01.adr, the yeti body the fork's wave Yeti 46010 wears; 4547 sh_standard_yeti_01.adr is a banner with no skeleton, the Frosty Yeti starter's look."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "rc-0137 prize wheel: fandom 'Hot Springs Haven' (revision 48945) lists one prize wheel per combat job and a 49-coin slot; any other job spins the items every job's wheel holds. Brawler: the wiki's 'Bell Brawler Gloves' is 'Saved by the Bell Brawler Gloves' in our record dungeons/hot_springs_haven.json."
    }
  ]
